  "question": {
    "text": "Let a line having direction ratios <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;intersect the lines&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;at the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>. Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;is equal to"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "84",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#956;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>DR&#39;s&nbsp;of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>i.e.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Also&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn></math></p><p>After solving above two equations, we get&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>i.e.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>84</mn></math></p>"
  }
}